WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.328 --> 00:00:04.841
- What's up Believe Nation,
today I'm going to talk

00:00:04.841 --> 00:00:07.503
about seven essential tools that all

00:00:07.503 --> 00:00:09.340
entrepreneurs should know about.

00:00:09.340 --> 00:00:10.594
And as always guys, if you hear

00:00:10.594 --> 00:00:11.871
a point that really resonates with you,

00:00:11.871 --> 00:00:13.768
please leave it down
in the comments below,

00:00:13.768 --> 00:00:14.859
put quotes around it so other people

00:00:14.859 --> 00:00:16.379
can be inspired as well.

00:00:16.379 --> 00:00:18.448
And also, writing it down helps you lock

00:00:18.448 --> 00:00:19.781
it in for yourself too.

00:00:19.781 --> 00:00:20.952
Enjoy.

00:00:20.952 --> 00:00:24.619
- [Male Robotic Voice]
Nine, eight, seven...

00:00:28.630 --> 00:00:30.282
- So I often get asked by entrepreneurs,

00:00:30.282 --> 00:00:31.777
what tools do you use, what are some

00:00:31.777 --> 00:00:34.049
of the most impactful, resourceful tools

00:00:34.049 --> 00:00:36.040
that you put into practice every day

00:00:36.040 --> 00:00:37.471
to help you build your business?

00:00:37.471 --> 00:00:39.210
And what should I apply in my company

00:00:39.210 --> 00:00:40.849
to help me grow faster?

00:00:40.849 --> 00:00:42.414
And so today, I'm going to share with you

00:00:42.414 --> 00:00:44.400
my seven tools that I
think every entrepreneur

00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:47.307
should be aware of and
using in their company.

00:00:47.307 --> 00:00:50.640
(urban hip hop music)

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:52.071
Tool number one is a calendar,

00:00:52.071 --> 00:00:53.514
and this is the most basic of all

00:00:53.514 --> 00:00:55.375
the tools that I'm going
to talk about today.

00:00:55.375 --> 00:00:57.391
A calendar, whether
you're using your Outlook,

00:00:57.391 --> 00:00:58.840
whether you're using your Google Calendar,

00:00:58.840 --> 00:01:00.829
whether you're using a physical calendar,

00:01:00.829 --> 00:01:03.487
a calendar is so, so, so, so important.

00:01:03.487 --> 00:01:04.581
But more important than just having

00:01:04.581 --> 00:01:08.302
a calendar is sticking
to it and abiding by it.

00:01:08.302 --> 00:01:09.692
How many times do you set something

00:01:09.692 --> 00:01:11.730
in your calendar, not a
meeting with somebody else,

00:01:11.730 --> 00:01:13.140
I think with meetings, you're more likely

00:01:13.140 --> 00:01:15.131
to go to it 'cause you
commit to somebody else.

00:01:15.131 --> 00:01:16.530
But you put something in your calendar,

00:01:16.530 --> 00:01:18.050
and then you don't stick to it.

00:01:18.050 --> 00:01:19.250
You put something down and say,

00:01:19.250 --> 00:01:21.211
I'm going to work on my
business in this time chunk,

00:01:21.211 --> 00:01:24.059
and then something comes up
and you don't stick to it

00:01:24.059 --> 00:01:26.242
and you don't keep it as a priority.

00:01:26.242 --> 00:01:28.622
And so, one, it's having the discipline

00:01:28.622 --> 00:01:30.552
and the patience to actually stick to it,

00:01:30.552 --> 00:01:33.461
and two, it's making a
calendar that makes sense.

00:01:33.461 --> 00:01:35.650
And so, every month on a small scale,

00:01:35.650 --> 00:01:37.418
and every quarter on a bigger scale,

00:01:37.418 --> 00:01:39.492
I'll look at my calendar,
I'll see where I'm

00:01:39.492 --> 00:01:41.370
spending my time on different activities

00:01:41.370 --> 00:01:44.060
and think, is this the
best use of my time?

00:01:44.060 --> 00:01:46.020
Is there something else
that I want to work on,

00:01:46.020 --> 00:01:48.145
and then if I add that to my calendar,

00:01:48.145 --> 00:01:49.489
what gets taken away?

00:01:49.489 --> 00:01:51.907
And so, most days when I wake up,

00:01:51.907 --> 00:01:54.370
I'm just applying what I
wrote down in my calendar.

00:01:54.370 --> 00:01:56.210
It's just work mode, grind mode,

00:01:56.210 --> 00:01:58.827
I'm not thinking high-level strategic,

00:01:58.827 --> 00:02:00.215
what should be in my calendar?

00:02:00.215 --> 00:02:01.951
'Cause if you're thinking
like that every day,

00:02:01.951 --> 00:02:04.050
if every day is just,
how am I going to plan,

00:02:04.050 --> 00:02:05.910
how am I going to plan,
you don't ever take action.

00:02:05.910 --> 00:02:08.137
We have to take action as an entrepreneur.

00:02:08.137 --> 00:02:10.930
So most days I'm waking up
and I'm just taking action

00:02:10.930 --> 00:02:12.429
and living according to the calendar

00:02:12.429 --> 00:02:13.721
that I set up for myself.

00:02:13.721 --> 00:02:15.251
And then once a month or once a quarter,

00:02:15.251 --> 00:02:17.316
I'll look at it, and it's like hmm,

00:02:17.316 --> 00:02:19.750
that time there, that's not
really being spent effectively,

00:02:19.750 --> 00:02:21.387
and I want to add this new thing in,

00:02:21.387 --> 00:02:22.710
so I need to find a spot for it.

00:02:22.710 --> 00:02:24.426
So let's shift things around.

00:02:24.426 --> 00:02:26.548
And so, making a good calendar

00:02:26.548 --> 00:02:28.440
that works for you,
works for your schedule,

00:02:28.440 --> 00:02:30.831
works for what you want to
accomplish with your goals,

00:02:30.831 --> 00:02:32.707
and then sticking to it is one

00:02:32.707 --> 00:02:33.810
of the most important resources

00:02:33.810 --> 00:02:35.856
that you can use as an entrepreneur.

00:02:35.856 --> 00:02:39.301
(urban hip hop music)

00:02:39.301 --> 00:02:40.768
Number two is Upwork.

00:02:40.768 --> 00:02:43.139
Upwork.com is a website that freelancers

00:02:43.139 --> 00:02:45.239
from around the world can sign up to,

00:02:45.239 --> 00:02:47.779
and you can use them to
bid on your projects.

00:02:47.779 --> 00:02:49.074
A lot of times, people
think when they have

00:02:49.074 --> 00:02:50.829
to hire somebody, they need somebody local

00:02:50.829 --> 00:02:52.571
and it needs to be somebody full-time.

00:02:52.571 --> 00:02:55.331
Or you can get people highly-talented,

00:02:55.331 --> 00:02:57.772
highly-skilled who are working overseas

00:02:57.772 --> 00:02:59.653
who will work part-time for you

00:02:59.653 --> 00:03:01.682
and a set number of hours and it will be

00:03:01.682 --> 00:03:04.208
a lot cheaper than hiring somebody local

00:03:04.208 --> 00:03:07.869
to do amazing, amazing,
amazing work for you.

00:03:07.869 --> 00:03:09.406
And recognize you can't do this alone,

00:03:09.406 --> 00:03:11.677
and so having a team of people around you

00:03:11.677 --> 00:03:13.406
who can help complement your weaknesses

00:03:13.406 --> 00:03:16.386
and do amazing things for your
company is really important.

00:03:16.386 --> 00:03:18.059
I think the hiring process is broken

00:03:18.059 --> 00:03:18.892
for a lot of companies.

00:03:18.892 --> 00:03:20.837
I'm a big fan of bringing people

00:03:20.837 --> 00:03:24.186
on on a trial basis, letting
them see what they can do,

00:03:24.186 --> 00:03:26.462
seeing more in their
results, 'cause I don't think

00:03:26.462 --> 00:03:28.217
a job interview and a resume really

00:03:28.217 --> 00:03:30.057
speaks to somebody's results.

00:03:30.057 --> 00:03:31.936
If you're hiring a video editor

00:03:31.936 --> 00:03:33.537
as an example, their ability to write

00:03:33.537 --> 00:03:36.090
a resume and to do well in a job interview

00:03:36.090 --> 00:03:37.287
has nothing to do with their ability

00:03:37.287 --> 00:03:39.212
to actually make good videos.

00:03:39.212 --> 00:03:40.776
And so I'd much rather skip a lot

00:03:40.776 --> 00:03:43.113
of this stuff and move to,
okay let's start working

00:03:43.113 --> 00:03:44.804
on trial project and see what you can do

00:03:44.804 --> 00:03:46.600
in a couple of hours work.

00:03:46.600 --> 00:03:48.614
I made a video called The
Hiring Process is Broken.

00:03:48.614 --> 00:03:49.656
I recommend you go check that out

00:03:49.656 --> 00:03:51.195
'cause it has a lot of those steps

00:03:51.195 --> 00:03:52.134
in a lot more detail.

00:03:52.134 --> 00:03:53.516
Being able to bring on good people

00:03:53.516 --> 00:03:55.217
from around the world who can help you

00:03:55.217 --> 00:03:56.712
build your big mission and achieve

00:03:56.712 --> 00:03:58.645
your goals in a cost-effective way

00:03:58.645 --> 00:04:00.195
and on a part-time basis is such

00:04:00.195 --> 00:04:02.636
an amazing resource for
you, and so I highly

00:04:02.636 --> 00:04:04.393
recommend checking out Upwork.

00:04:04.393 --> 00:04:07.722
(urban hip hop music)

00:04:07.722 --> 00:04:09.374
Number three is 99designs.

00:04:09.374 --> 00:04:11.972
This is similar to Upwork,
but just for design.

00:04:11.972 --> 00:04:13.521
And so what happens is, you can create

00:04:13.521 --> 00:04:15.580
a project that you need
for your design work,

00:04:15.580 --> 00:04:17.699
whether it's a new logo,
a new website design,

00:04:17.699 --> 00:04:20.623
banners, flyers,
brochures, business cards,

00:04:20.623 --> 00:04:22.779
whatever it is that needs to be designed,

00:04:22.779 --> 00:04:24.290
if you are not a designer yourself,

00:04:24.290 --> 00:04:26.132
you can put it up on 99designs,

00:04:26.132 --> 00:04:28.223
they recommend different pricing points,

00:04:28.223 --> 00:04:30.362
and people from around
the world will bid on it.

00:04:30.362 --> 00:04:33.064
And they'll bid on it with designs.

00:04:33.064 --> 00:04:34.823
And so you can structure your content

00:04:34.823 --> 00:04:37.334
so that you only pay if you're getting

00:04:37.334 --> 00:04:39.212
a design that you actually like.

00:04:39.212 --> 00:04:40.261
And so people will bid on it,

00:04:40.261 --> 00:04:41.893
they'll submit designs, you give feedback,

00:04:41.893 --> 00:04:43.814
you go back and forth,
until you get something

00:04:43.814 --> 00:04:46.093
that you love and say yes, that's it.

00:04:46.093 --> 00:04:47.980
I think a lot of times,
the way that we hire

00:04:47.980 --> 00:04:49.614
designers can also be broken.

00:04:49.614 --> 00:04:52.652
Typically, it's you look at a portfolio

00:04:52.652 --> 00:04:54.796
and say well here's what
we've done in the past.

00:04:54.796 --> 00:04:56.662
It doesn't mean that I'm
going to get something good.

00:04:56.662 --> 00:04:57.883
Just because you've done this kind

00:04:57.883 --> 00:04:59.129
of work in the past, it doesn't mean

00:04:59.129 --> 00:05:01.372
that what you're going to give
me is going to be amazing.

00:05:01.372 --> 00:05:02.732
The best way to figure it out is

00:05:02.732 --> 00:05:04.492
to actually get involved in a project

00:05:04.492 --> 00:05:05.903
and start doing it.

00:05:05.903 --> 00:05:07.181
The challenge of hiring somebody locally

00:05:07.181 --> 00:05:09.917
is you pick one person,
it's going to be expensive,

00:05:09.917 --> 00:05:12.106
and you don't know if you're
going to get a great result.

00:05:12.106 --> 00:05:13.640
Where with a website like 99designs,

00:05:13.640 --> 00:05:14.866
you get people from around the world,

00:05:14.866 --> 00:05:17.524
you'll get dozens to hundreds of designs

00:05:17.524 --> 00:05:19.198
and you can tweak and go back and forth

00:05:19.198 --> 00:05:20.928
until you get the one you actually,

00:05:20.928 --> 00:05:24.060
actually, actually love and
want to use in your business.

00:05:24.060 --> 00:05:25.518
And so another great tool to use,

00:05:25.518 --> 00:05:28.359
I highly recommend for any
design work, 99designs.

00:05:28.359 --> 00:05:32.088
(urban hip hop music)

00:05:32.088 --> 00:05:34.388
The number four resource is YouTube.

00:05:34.388 --> 00:05:36.221
We're all here watching on YouTube.

00:05:36.221 --> 00:05:37.617
And it's no surprise for me,

00:05:37.617 --> 00:05:40.758
it's both as a creator and
then also as a resource.

00:05:40.758 --> 00:05:42.088
I think if you're a creator, you have

00:05:42.088 --> 00:05:43.787
a chance to tell your story, to promote

00:05:43.787 --> 00:05:46.096
your business, to talk
about behind the scenes,

00:05:46.096 --> 00:05:48.598
why you started this, how
you do certain things.

00:05:48.598 --> 00:05:51.486
I think every entrepreneur
should at least consider

00:05:51.486 --> 00:05:53.795
being on YouTube as a
part of their business.

00:05:53.795 --> 00:05:56.240
Whether YouTube becomes your business

00:05:56.240 --> 00:05:58.931
or it's just a funnel for your business,

00:05:58.931 --> 00:06:02.376
for my company, for Evan
Carmichael, Incorporated,

00:06:02.376 --> 00:06:03.975
a lot of the opportunities that I get

00:06:03.975 --> 00:06:07.067
for my company come through
the YouTube channel.

00:06:07.067 --> 00:06:09.864
For Toronto Dance Salsa, we're
posting videos every week

00:06:09.864 --> 00:06:13.355
on our YouTube channel, and
that drive students more.

00:06:13.355 --> 00:06:15.402
The model's not revenue off of YouTube,

00:06:15.402 --> 00:06:17.251
but students coming to the class,

00:06:17.251 --> 00:06:18.964
because now they're aware
of what we're doing.

00:06:18.964 --> 00:06:21.008
I think it's a fantastic
marking opportunity

00:06:21.008 --> 00:06:23.562
for any entrepreneur
because so many people

00:06:23.562 --> 00:06:27.152
are on YouTube and people
want to know your story.

00:06:27.152 --> 00:06:28.777
Your competitive advantage as an

00:06:28.777 --> 00:06:31.221
entrepreneur is your story.

00:06:31.221 --> 00:06:33.218
The way you beat the big
guys in your industry

00:06:33.218 --> 00:06:36.443
is not going to be on price, it's
not going to be on reputation,

00:06:36.443 --> 00:06:38.007
it's going to be on your story.

00:06:38.007 --> 00:06:40.866
I feel connected to you, I
feel like you just care more,

00:06:40.866 --> 00:06:43.646
and you can't really communicate care more

00:06:43.646 --> 00:06:45.246
if you have a boring website.

00:06:45.246 --> 00:06:46.387
And an easy way to do it, is get in front

00:06:46.387 --> 00:06:49.077
of a camera and just talk.

00:06:49.077 --> 00:06:50.377
You don't have to be
great and you don't need

00:06:50.377 --> 00:06:51.873
to have fantastic gear.

00:06:51.873 --> 00:06:53.672
The most important thing is the message

00:06:53.672 --> 00:06:56.160
that I feel the passion
and the connection to you

00:06:56.160 --> 00:06:57.596
and why you started this business.

00:06:57.596 --> 00:06:58.681
So that's from the creator's side.

00:06:58.681 --> 00:07:00.286
I think from a learning point of view,

00:07:00.286 --> 00:07:01.825
it's also really helpful.

00:07:01.825 --> 00:07:04.367
A lot of the best learning
that I've received

00:07:04.367 --> 00:07:06.838
in my life has come from
my own YouTube channel.

00:07:06.838 --> 00:07:08.566
I mean it's why I started
my YouTube channel.

00:07:08.566 --> 00:07:10.822
I wanted to learn as well for myself.

00:07:10.822 --> 00:07:12.436
I wanted to study these
famous entrepreneurs

00:07:12.436 --> 00:07:14.706
and learn from them because I didn't have

00:07:14.706 --> 00:07:16.726
connections to famous entrepreneurs.

00:07:16.726 --> 00:07:18.102
There was nobody in my family who was

00:07:18.102 --> 00:07:20.096
a successful entrepreneur, and so I wanted

00:07:20.096 --> 00:07:22.046
to hang around these people,
I knew it was important,

00:07:22.046 --> 00:07:23.605
I didn't know how to go out and do it,

00:07:23.605 --> 00:07:26.179
so I thought I'm going to make
a YouTube channel about it.

00:07:26.179 --> 00:07:28.311
And every time we profile
a famous entrepreneur,

00:07:28.311 --> 00:07:30.758
I review the videos, I review the content.

00:07:30.758 --> 00:07:33.345
I only put it up because
I have learned something

00:07:33.345 --> 00:07:34.486
from these videos, and it's been

00:07:34.486 --> 00:07:36.756
the single greatest source of education

00:07:36.756 --> 00:07:38.751
that has helped me as an entrepreneur

00:07:38.751 --> 00:07:41.804
is by watching my own videos every day.

00:07:41.804 --> 00:07:43.647
And so I think whether
you're watching my videos

00:07:43.647 --> 00:07:44.726
or whether you're trying to learn

00:07:44.726 --> 00:07:46.947
a certain skill, YouTube is a fantastic

00:07:46.947 --> 00:07:50.781
free resource that wasn't
available in the past.

00:07:50.781 --> 00:07:52.955
I wish I had this when I
was going to high school,

00:07:52.955 --> 00:07:54.904
because it can dramatically
short-cut your path

00:07:54.904 --> 00:07:57.065
to learning something,
as well as connect you

00:07:57.065 --> 00:07:59.350
to people who actually know
what they're talking about,

00:07:59.350 --> 00:08:01.614
connect you to experts in certain fields

00:08:01.614 --> 00:08:03.195
that before you would have no access to.

00:08:03.195 --> 00:08:04.302
So I highly recommend whatever you want

00:08:04.302 --> 00:08:06.745
to learn, somebody's made
a YouTube video about it.

00:08:06.745 --> 00:08:10.315
(urban hip hop music)

00:08:10.315 --> 00:08:12.115
My number five resource for entrepreneurs

00:08:12.115 --> 00:08:14.479
is Snapchat, Facebook, and Instagram.

00:08:14.479 --> 00:08:15.937
I think these are really important tools

00:08:15.937 --> 00:08:17.574
to again help you tell your story.

00:08:17.574 --> 00:08:20.323
I think entrepreneurs need to learn how

00:08:20.323 --> 00:08:22.114
to tell their story better.

00:08:22.114 --> 00:08:23.891
I think YouTube, typically people look

00:08:23.891 --> 00:08:26.474
at as a more polished resource,

00:08:27.473 --> 00:08:30.035
so you make your video and
there's editing involved in it,

00:08:30.035 --> 00:08:31.393
and it's longer form.

00:08:31.393 --> 00:08:32.226
Where if you just want to film

00:08:32.226 --> 00:08:33.851
from your phone, you want
to get better practice,

00:08:33.851 --> 00:08:36.372
more experience, you can get on Snapchat,

00:08:36.372 --> 00:08:38.042
you can get on Instagram,
you can do the story,

00:08:38.042 --> 00:08:39.641
you can do Facebook with the Stories now.

00:08:39.641 --> 00:08:42.202
All three platforms allow
you to make really informal

00:08:42.202 --> 00:08:45.833
videos, it's expected to be informal.

00:08:45.833 --> 00:08:47.374
It's expected when you do Snapchat

00:08:47.374 --> 00:08:49.491
that people are coming from their phone,

00:08:49.491 --> 00:08:51.179
and it's expected to be more raw.

00:08:51.179 --> 00:08:52.102
It doesn't need to be produced,

00:08:52.102 --> 00:08:53.501
it doesn't need to be edited.

00:08:53.501 --> 00:08:57.652
And so, it's a great
tool to help you become

00:08:57.652 --> 00:08:59.771
a better storyteller, to help get your

00:08:59.771 --> 00:09:00.952
message out there more.

00:09:00.952 --> 00:09:03.121
And the good news is, for some of you,

00:09:03.121 --> 00:09:05.613
the stuff that you create
expires in 24 hours.

00:09:05.613 --> 00:09:07.791
I'm not a huge fan of it, because I want

00:09:07.791 --> 00:09:09.867
the stuff that I make to live forever.

00:09:09.867 --> 00:09:12.371
When I put love into
something, into these videos,

00:09:12.371 --> 00:09:14.130
I want it to live forever,
I want my grandkids

00:09:14.130 --> 00:09:15.682
to watch this and learn from it

00:09:15.682 --> 00:09:17.661
and it apply it to their
life and their business.

00:09:17.661 --> 00:09:18.972
I want to build a legacy.

00:09:18.972 --> 00:09:20.987
But if you're nervous and you're worried

00:09:20.987 --> 00:09:22.581
and you're not sure how
good you're going to be,

00:09:22.581 --> 00:09:23.983
and you don't want everybody to see

00:09:23.983 --> 00:09:27.054
it and to live forever,
then get on Snapchat

00:09:27.054 --> 00:09:29.123
and get on Instagram Stories, because

00:09:29.123 --> 00:09:31.731
the stories disappear in 24 hours.

00:09:31.731 --> 00:09:34.371
When I took over Toronto Dance Salsa,

00:09:34.371 --> 00:09:36.666
I wanted Alex who's
helping me run the company

00:09:36.666 --> 00:09:38.234
to get good at storytelling.

00:09:38.234 --> 00:09:41.108
He had zero experience,
zero practice in this.

